[[Open This|2.4 Virtual private networks]]

---

https://docs.oxide.computer/guides/key-entities-and-concepts#_virtual_private_networks

[[VPC]]s are private [[RFC1918]] networks that isolate sets of instances from each other. Instances within a VPC subnet can talk to each other using private IP addresses (if firewall rules allow it) but traffic between VPCs must go through external IPs.
